Z||000015||ChopTop||10-04-2001||09:48 AM||||OK, here's my idea.  Paint it bright yellow, including the rub strip, spoiler (including the rubber stanchion seals) and ground effects.  Dark tinted windows and yellow lettering of SE or Formula on the sailpanel, yellow lettered windshield header.  For wheels you can't beat chrome or polished aluminum for attention.  If you want to funk it up you could go with gloss black wheels with yellow lugs, center cap, pinstripe around the lip, yellow calipers (or reverse the concept, yellow wheels, black lugs, etc).  Want more, go with some graphics on the lower portion of the ground effects, I'd go with a painted chrome look/black combo to tie everything in together.  I've read some folks are having custom painted graphics painted on *vinyl, when they get bored with the design they simply remove and install another custom painted graphic.  <BR>If you want the brightest yellow available ask your painter supply for Tone Yellow, (paint guys can correct me if I'm wrong).  I was told this is how it comes directly from the paint manufacturers, no additives.  This is the base color used to match paints. Just keep some cleaner on hand because insects are very attracted to it.<BR>*The vinyl I was referring to is the type that is being applied to cars.  If I understand the concept correctly, the vinyl is fist applied to the car in the desired pattern, and then the custom painted graphic is applied directly to it.  Couple pluses to this idea, it allows people to follow faddish graphic styles and colors from year to year, or update their car every few years without resorted to having the whole car painted again. And also allows you to still have an original graphic design.    <BR><p>[This message has been edited by ChopTop (edited 10-04-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000016||StuGood||10-04-2001||09:57 AM||||Purple and green, without a doubt...<P>looks awful.  Sorry - you asked.<P>And since you asked, I think the yellow/ black one is a little, well, haphazard.  It needs something to "tie it all together."  Either make the spoiler yellow, or leave the spoiler black, and make the hood + rear decklid black to match. Something like that.  JMHO   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">     <p>[This message has been edited by StuGood (edited 10-04-2001).]||||reg||13
