Z||000035||MinnGreenGT||10-04-2001||02:10 PM|||| <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/86sepurple01.jpg"> <BR>I would suggest that the wing is OK in yellow, as is the door trim moldings.  But on the lower aero effects, I'd consider doing just the lower part in yellow (below door line) but the part at door level to leave purple.... just a suggestion.  BTW: I'd probably do the roof line in purple to match.||||reg||1
Z||000036||LZeitgeist||10-04-2001||02:12 PM||||Cheever - LOL!!!!! I love it...   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Others - It's not the purple I don't like... it's not the green I don't like... it's that purple and that green *together* I don't like. <P>I've seen more than one really sweet-looking purple Fiero. Hell, the all-flourescent green one up there actually looks pretty dang good, except I think neon colors fade really quickly in a year or so, don't they?<P>But even the purple/yellow idea makes me want to gag... Yuck. &lt;bleah&gt; - it may work in Graphic Arts, but it screams "RICER!!!!!" on a car, whether it's on a Civic or a Ferrari, or anything in between.<P>Hey, I'm all for individuality... and as was said earier, as long as *YOU* are happy, who gives a flip what *we* say?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  But you asked for opinions, and so here they are... jeweltone colors (like metallic purple, or royal blue, or metallic red) usually end up looking pretty cheesy when they're accented with solid, non-metallic colors (like sun yellow or neon green). It seems to say "expensive factory-quality paint job + cheap-a$$ Speedy Sign*A*Rama shop vinyl stripes = no sense of aesthetics = looking *desperately* for attention/any attention/good or bad".<P>Just my two cents...   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <P><BR>EDIT - hell, the more I look at it, that fluorescent green/black one up there is looking better and better... 8)<p>[This message has been edited by LZeitgeist (edited 10-04-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000037||MinnGreenGT||10-04-2001||02:29 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by LZeitgeist:<BR><B>But even the purple/yellow idea makes me want to gag... Yuck. &lt;bleah&gt; - it may work in Graphic Arts, but it screams "RICER!!!!!" on a car, whether it's on a Civic or a Ferrari, or anything in between.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Ummm... have you ever seen John Norman's Obsession? Purple/Yellow will pretty much always work together (if done correctly) ...even a dark blue/yellow looks great! (ever see a '98 Corvette Pace Car?)  Corvette=ricer? I don't think so.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/98vettepc1.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/98vettepc2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
