Z||000049||86seyellow||10-04-2001||04:57 PM||||And to finish if off, Clear TaighlightS?? DO you think the lotus look is ok<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000050||MinnGreenGT||10-04-2001||05:07 PM||||clear taillights are easy for the coupe... I can help with the lens, you'll have to dig around for the colored bulbs.  Yes, I actually like the "Lotus-Look" when it comes to the emblem on the driver's side fender... I may do that the next time I repaint the car.<P>One more thing... instead of doing the center in yellow, you can get the wheels refinished at Precision Wheel Service (Richfield, MN) for about $95-100 ea. and have them turn and polish the metal, and re-coat the inside of the "fins" with yellow instead of black.  They're the same company that worked on Kev's and my rims (as well as many others in the area).<p>[This message has been edited by MinnGreenGT (edited 10-04-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000051||86seyellow||10-04-2001||05:15 PM||||Well Ok, this is it .<P>The car will be purple like Fomula did with a purple wing. Yellow ground effects and racing stripes on hood and wing from MinnGreenGt. It will have the Lotus look Fiero emblem on the bottom. Yellow mirrors and door moulding. Clear taighlights with purple or yellow bulbs? I will have to decide on the rims after it is painted.But for now the vette rims will have a yellow center cap to start with. Any one have an estimate on the job. I am guessing $3000. <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fieropix1_copy1.jpg">    <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/86seyellow_01.jpg">  <P>I can go as fast as I want unless I get caught||||reg||1
Z||000052||MinnGreenGT||10-04-2001||05:44 PM||||My only suggestion is this: Quality.  Make sure you use the best paint, especailly if you're using metallic purple (possibly check with the "<A HREF="http://www.houseofkolor.com/" TARGET=_blank>house of kolor</A>" for the best).  Make sure they add the "flex agent" to the paint (this will help reduce paint cracks from minor impacts).  If possible, a body-off paint job is best. At minimum they need to remove all the moldings and the gasket around the windshield (that's where my paint is chipping).  And either replace your dew-strips during a body-off painting, or be posative they don't paint them.  And a couple layers of clear coat... even throw some fine gold pearl in the purple- anything to make it sparkle that little bit more.<P>As for your wheels... I suspect that after you finish your repaint you'll decide that it's time for some nice high-polish chrome wheels. But only time will tell.<P>It's all good as long as you're sure you'll like it!  And anyone is always welcome to get-togethers and cruises!<p>[This message has been edited by MinnGreenGT (edited 10-04-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000053||gargoyle||10-04-2001||05:50 PM||||Well I may be too late but if you want different and very NOT rice, how about candy apple red. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> Now that is a color that you can get to really look deep. You could do black or silver as a contrast color. Hey Minn, you want to try that one as a color. I'm glad you are keeping the wheels, they look good and are also different. ||||reg||6
